  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The third-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}+\\frac{1}{t}\\,{y}^{″}-{t}^{2}{y}^{′}=\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t)$ and ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$",
